    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0618" n="534" xml:id="pg534"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Raikes.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Chargé</hi>: Acting in the direction
                    indicated by your personal note of the 28th ultimo, certified copies of the
                    documents in the Russian and French languages, of which translations were
                    appended to the case of the United States, together with certified copies of
                    certain diplomatic correspondence in the English language, also appended, will
                    go in to-morrow’s pouch for delivery to Mr. Sifton through the United States
                    embassy at London.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear Mr. Raikes, very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
